# No new friend class

Do not add `friend class` or `friend struct` in new or edited code.

Existing friends stay where they are. Do not remove or rewrite them as part of an unrelated change:

- `cpp-lib/include/asn-buf.h` (`friend class AsnBuf`)
- vendored `cpp-lib/jsoncpp/`

## What to do instead

When one type needs to call another type's private operation, keep the operation private and pass a callback the owning type installs. The owner creates that callback in a member function, so the callback can reach private members. The collaborator stores and invokes the callback. It does not become a friend.

A public method is appropriate only when callers outside that collaboration are meant to use it.
